 85 year  old man the first is someone who had not  committed an earlier offender has spent  a lot of time in public service all of  that is factored in generally at  sentencing and indeed President Trump  could have simply negated the sentence  he could have allowed this to go forward  if he did that our pile could could  appeal his conviction but not face any  jail time  those are the types of things that the  Justice Department weighs in on as they  go to a president say look these are  your options but I have to say I would  be very surprised if the professionals  at the Justice Department would have  recommended this pardon I would expect  the president would have gotten a great  deal of opposition from the Justice  Department these people have got to go  into court and they tell judges we will  comply with what you say this part does  not say that thank you thank you  Jonathan didn't mean to cut you off  there running out of time we appreciate  the perspective thank you
 

